==============================================================================
PART A -- on the EVEN/LINEAR side, VC is just the dimension, and the shattered
          sets are the INDEPENDENT SETS OF A MATROID.  For the cut space of K_n
          (= the switching group) that matroid is graphic: shattered = FORESTS.
==============================================================================
  n  edges  cut dim  VC(cut)  shattered = forests?  cycle dim  VC(cycle)  brute agrees
  3      3        2        2                  True          1          1          True
  4      6        3        3                  True          3          3          True
  5     10        4        4                  True          6          6          True
  6     15        5        5                  True         10         10          True

  So every SWITCHING CLASS (a coset of the cut space) has VC = n-1 exactly,
  with the forests of K_n as its shattered sets -- translation cannot change
  surjectivity of a projection, so cosets and the code agree.

==============================================================================
PART B -- on the ODD/NONLINEAR side, VC is a real combinatorial quantity
==============================================================================
  n  classes  floor(log2 n)  max VC              VC distribution  max Schutte k
  3        2              1       1                     [(1, 2)]              1
  4        4              2       2             [(1, 2), (2, 2)]              1
  5       12              2       2            [(1, 2), (2, 10)]              1
  6       56              2       2            [(1, 2), (2, 54)]              1
  7      456              2       2           [(1, 2), (2, 454)]              2

  Upper bound is immediate: shattering a k-set needs 2^k distinct patterns and
  there are only n vertices, so VC <= floor(log2 n).
  Lower bound by construction: put a TRANSITIVE tournament on S = {0..k-1}, whose
  in-S out-neighbourhoods are the k distinct nested sets {1..k-1} ... {} ; assign
  the remaining 2^k - k patterns freely to outside vertices.  So max VC = floor(log2 n).

  explicit n=8 witness: VC = 3 (floor(log2 8) = 3), code = 202356

==============================================================================
PART C -- where does VC sit in the invariant tiers?
==============================================================================
  n=4: VC changes under switching for 4/4 classes => switching-invariant? False
  n=5: VC changes under switching for 12/12 classes => switching-invariant? False
  n=6: VC changes under switching for 22/56 classes => switching-invariant? False
  n=7: VC changes under switching for 42/456 classes => switching-invariant? False

SUMMARY -- the high-leverage answer
  LINEARITY TRIVIALISES VC.  On the even/linear side (cut space = switching group,
  cycle space = even graphs) VC equals the dimension and the shattered sets are
  matroid independent sets -- forests, for the switching group.  Nothing new is
  measured.  On the odd/nonlinear side VC is bounded by floor(log2 n), attains it,
  and varies across tournaments.  THM-1420 says the odd side admits NO F_2-linear
  invariants, so it can never be pushed into the trivial linear case.
